[120.22616, "o", "65 paths discovered\r\n"]
[120.287782, "o", "\r\n"]
[121.290894, "o", "  \u001b[1m3. TUI\u001b[0m — Interactive Console\r\n     \u001b[0;32msplice-tui --devices-dir devices\u001b[0m\r\n     \u001b[2mTabbed interface: Devices, Paths, Telemetry, Status, Operations, Jobs\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m4. MCP Server\u001b[0m — AI Agent Interface\r\n"]
[121.290989, "o", "     \u001b[2mThe bridge exposes MCP tools for AI agents. Let's talk to Claude:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;32m$ \u001b[0mclaude -p \"Hello Claude! I have Splice running for our\r\n  Adtran Teraflex transponder. Can you connect to it and tell me\r\n  the current Q-factor and signal quality?\r\n"]
[121.291099, "o", "  Device: 192.0.2.92, port 830, username admin,\r\n  password is in devices/<device>/password.\"\r\n"]
[166.521211, "o", "Here's the Teraflex transponder's current signal quality snapshot:\r\n\r\n### Signal Quality Metrics\r\n\r\n| Metric | Value | Unit |\r\n|--------|-------|------|\r\n| **Q-Factor** | **13.8** | dB |\r\n| **SNR** | **20.9** | dB |\r\n| **OSNR** | **34.8** | dB |\r\n| **Optical Receive Power** | **-6.7** | dBm |\r\n| **Carrier Frequency Offset** | -0.002 | GHz |\r\n| **Polarization Dependent Loss** | 0.2 | dB |\r\n| **Differential Group Delay** | 3 | ps |\r\n| **SOP Tracking** | 0 | krad/s |\r\n\r\nThe link looks healthy — a Q-factor of **13.8 dB** is well above the 200G 16QAM FEC threshold (typically ~8.5 dB for SD-FEC), giving you roughly **5+ dB of margin**. The OSNR at 34.8 dB is excellent, and the received power of -6.7 dBm is in a comfortable range. PDL and DGD are both negligible.\r\n"]
[166.830365, "o", "\u001b[<u\u001b[?1004l\u001b[?2004l\u001b[?25h\u001b]9;4;0;\u0007\u001b]0;\u0007"]
[166.830442, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[166.870618, "o", "\r\n"]
[169.873735, "o", "\r\n\u001b[0;34m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;34m  ACT 7: Summary\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[169.87398, "o", "\u001b[0;34m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[170.876705, "o", "  \u001b[1mThree NETCONF-only devices, bridged to gNMI:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[0;32m●\u001b[0m  Lumentum ROADM     \u001b[2m192.0.2.17\u001b[0m  →  gNMI :9341\r\n    \u001b[0;32m●\u001b[0m  Adtran Teraflex    \u001b[2m192.0.2.92\u001b[0m  →  gNMI :9340\r\n    \u001b[0;32m●\u001b[0m  Juniper ILA        \u001b[2m192.0.2.20\u001b[0m  →  gNMI :9342\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mBy the numbers:\u001b[0m\r\n    • 3 vendors, 3 device types\r\n    • 19,000+ telemetry paths\r\n    • 504 tests\r\n    • 4 interfaces: CLI, Python API, TUI, MCP\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mNo changes to the devices. No vendor-specific adapters.\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mJust YANG model discovery and automatic catalog building.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
